  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;subversion&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The palace&apos;s subversion took barely twenty minutes at first light, with rebel columns forcing the bronze gates and marching the ministers out into the square at bayonet point.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">The millers blamed their scales&apos; subversion on thirty years of hard use, each season of grinding wear pulling the balance arm a few more grams away from true.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">Trustees applauded the endowment&apos;s subversion of the scholarship fund, which had doubled the number of students it could carry in five years.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The registry&apos;s subversion escaped six audits: a senior clerk time-stamped favored claims a day early, so every dispute went, by the book, his patrons&apos; way.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Subversion means the weakening or overthrowing of a system from within by quiet, indirect means, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because rebel columns forcing the gates is open assault from outside — nothing quiet, nothing indirect, nothing working through the palace&apos;s own machinery.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Subversion means the weakening or overthrowing of a system from within by quiet, indirect means, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because drifting scales are wear, not work — no one is doing anything, and subversion needs a subverter with a purpose.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Subversion means the weakening or overthrowing of a system from within by quiet, indirect means, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because an endowment that doubles a fund&apos;s reach is strengthening it — the writer wants subvention, financial support, a near-twin in spelling that points the opposite way.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Subversion means the weakening or overthrowing of a system from within by quiet, indirect means, so it&apos;s the correct answer because the registry&apos;s own clerk used the registry&apos;s own stamps — every ruling lawful on its face, and the whole system quietly aimed at his patrons.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
